+## MCP effects
+
+Confirm destructive changes with the user before calling a tool. Overwriting settings, replacing traffic weights, prices or availability, enabling advertising spend, and irreversible sends such as feedback or event retries have destructive effects even when they can later be changed again. Generic API tools cover every reachable endpoint; use the actual operation's effects, not its HTTP method, to assess a request. Selector POST lookups can be read-only; report-job creation is a write.
+
